Feature: Databricks PySpark script to transfer eligible files from Vendor S3 to Purgo S3

  The script transfers files from the vendor's S3 bucket to the Purgo S3 folder, based on configuration in purgo_playground.ingest_config_master, only for active configurations (active_flag = "A"). 
  Files are only transferred if they do not exist in either the Purgo S3 folder or the Archive S3 folder. 
  S3 paths are dynamically retrieved from ingest_config_master. 
  AWS credentials are securely accessed from Databricks secrets under scope "aws_keys".

  Background:
    Given the Databricks Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks"
    And the Unity Catalog schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the configuration table is "purgo_playground.ingest_config_master"
    And AWS credentials are retrieved from Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" with keys "access_key" and "secret_key"

  Scenario: Retrieve S3 folder paths from ingest_config_master for active configurations
    Given ingest_config_master contains the following rows:
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | 1         | s3://vendor-bucket/folder1/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing1/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archive1/    | A           |
      | 2         | s3://vendor-bucket/folder2/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing2/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archive2/    | I           |
    When the script queries ingest_config_master for all rows where active_flag = "A"
    Then it should retrieve:
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                |
      | 1         | s3://vendor-bucket/folder1/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing1/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archive1/    |

  Scenario Outline: Transfer eligible files from Vendor S3 to Purgo S3
    Given the configuration row has:
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path              | s3_landing_path              | s3_archive_path              | active_flag |
      | <config_id> | <s3_vendor_path>            | <s3_landing_path>            | <s3_archive_path>            | A           |
    And the Vendor S3 folder contains files:
      | file_name         |
      | <vendor_file_1>   |
      | <vendor_file_2>   |
      | <vendor_file_3>   |
    And the Purgo S3 folder contains files:
      | file_name         |
      | <purgo_file_1>    |
      | <purgo_file_2>    |
    And the Archive S3 folder contains files:
      | file_name         |
      | <archive_file_1>  |
      | <archive_file_2>  |
    When the script compares file names in Vendor S3 with those in Purgo S3 and Archive S3 (case-sensitive, full match, including extension)
    Then it should transfer only files from Vendor S3 that do not exist in either Purgo S3 or Archive S3 to the Purgo S3 folder
    And the transferred files should be:
      | file_name         |
      | <expected_file_1> |
      | <expected_file_2> |

    Examples:
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path              | s3_landing_path              | s3_archive_path              | vendor_file_1 | vendor_file_2 | vendor_file_3 | purgo_file_1 | purgo_file_2 | archive_file_1 | archive_file_2 | expected_file_1 | expected_file_2 |
      | 1         | s3://vendor-bucket/folder1/ | s3://purgo-bucket/landing1/  | s3://purgo-bucket/archive1/  | fileA.csv     | fileB.csv     | fileC.csv     | fileB.csv    | fileD.csv    | fileE.csv      | fileC.csv      | fileA.csv       |                 |
      | 2         | s3://vendor-bucket/folder2/ | s3://purgo-bucket/landing2/  | s3://purgo-bucket/archive2/  | data1.txt     | data2.txt     | data3.txt     | data2.txt    |              | data3.txt      |                | data1.txt       |                 |

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if all Vendor files exist in Purgo or Archive
    Given the configuration row has:
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path              | s3_landing_path              | s3_archive_path              | active_flag |
      | 3         | s3://vendor-bucket/folder3/ | s3://purgo-bucket/landing3/  | s3://purgo-bucket/archive3/  | A           |
    And the Vendor S3 folder contains files:
      | file_name         |
      | fileX.csv         |
      | fileY.csv         |
    And the Purgo S3 folder contains files:
      | file_name         |
      | fileX.csv         |
    And the Archive S3 folder contains files:
      | file_name         |
      | fileY.csv         |
    When the script compares file names in Vendor S3 with those in Purgo S3 and Archive S3
    Then it should not transfer any files
    And the transferred files list should be empty

  Scenario: Only process configurations with active_flag = "A"
    Given ingest_config_master contains the following rows:
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | 4         | s3://vendor-bucket/folder4/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing4/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archive4/    | I           |
      | 5         | s3://vendor-bucket/folder5/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing5/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archive5/    | A           |
    When the script runs
    Then it should only process config_id "5"
    And it should not process config_id "4"

  Scenario: Error when AWS credentials are missing from Databricks secret
    Given the Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" does not contain "access_key" or "secret_key"
    When the script attempts to retrieve AWS credentials
    Then it should fail with error message "AWS credentials not found in Databricks secret scope 'aws_keys'"

  Scenario: Error when S3 path columns are missing in ingest_config_master
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with config_id "6" and active_flag "A"
    And the row has null values for s3_vendor_path, s3_landing_path, or s3_archive_path
    When the script attempts to retrieve S3 paths
    Then it should fail with error message "S3 path columns (s3_vendor_path, s3_landing_path, s3_archive_path) must not be null for active configuration"

  Scenario: Error when file transfer fails
    Given the script attempts to transfer file "fileZ.csv" from Vendor S3 to Purgo S3
    And the S3 API returns an error "AccessDenied"
    When the script processes the file
    Then it should log error "Failed to transfer fileZ.csv: AccessDenied"
    And the file should not be present in the Purgo S3 folder

  Scenario: File name matching is case-sensitive and includes extension
    Given the Vendor S3 folder contains files:
      | file_name         |
      | FileA.csv         |
      | filea.csv         |
    And the Purgo S3 folder contains files:
      | file_name         |
      | fileA.csv         |
    And the Archive S3 folder contains files:
      | file_name         |
      |                  |
    When the script compares file names
    Then it should transfer only "FileA.csv" (if not present in Purgo or Archive)
    And "filea.csv" should be transferred if not present in Purgo or Archive

  Scenario: File transfer is a copy, not a move (source file remains in Vendor S3)
    Given the script transfers "fileB.csv" from Vendor S3 to Purgo S3
    When the transfer is complete
    Then "fileB.csv" should exist in both Vendor S3 and Purgo S3

  Scenario: File transfer is recursive if file_recursive_flag = "Y"
    Given ingest_config_master row has file_recursive_flag = "Y"
    And the Vendor S3 folder contains subfolders with files:
      | subfolder   | file_name     |
      | sub1/       | file1.csv     |
      | sub2/       | file2.csv     |
    And the Purgo S3 and Archive S3 folders do not contain these files
    When the script runs
    Then it should transfer "sub1/file1.csv" and "sub2/file2.csv" to the Purgo S3 folder

  Scenario: File transfer is not recursive if file_recursive_flag is null or not "Y"
    Given ingest_config_master row has file_recursive_flag = null
    And the Vendor S3 folder contains:
      | file_name     |
      | file1.csv     |
      | sub1/file2.csv|
    When the script runs
    Then it should only consider "file1.csv" in the root of the Vendor S3 folder
    And "sub1/file2.csv" should not be transferred

  Scenario: Do not process inactive configurations
    Given ingest_config_master row has active_flag = "I"
    When the script runs
    Then it should skip this configuration

  Scenario: Error if ingest_config_master table is missing or inaccessible
    Given the table "purgo_playground.ingest_config_master" does not exist or cannot be queried
    When the script runs
    Then it should fail with error message "Configuration table purgo_playground.ingest_config_master not found or inaccessible"

  Scenario: Error if no active configurations are found
    Given ingest_config_master contains no rows with active_flag = "A"
    When the script runs
    Then it should fail with error message "No active configurations found in purgo_playground.ingest_config_master"

  Scenario: Log summary of transferred files
    Given the script transfers files:
      | file_name     | config_id |
      | fileA.csv     | 1         |
      | fileB.csv     | 1         |
    When the script completes
    Then it should log a summary:
      | config_id | transferred_files      |
      | 1         | fileA.csv, fileB.csv  |

  Scenario: Log error for files that could not be transferred
    Given the script attempts to transfer "fileC.csv" and encounters an error "NetworkTimeout"
    When the script completes
    Then it should log error "Failed to transfer fileC.csv: NetworkTimeout"

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if s3_vendor_path, s3_landing_path, or s3_archive_path is not a valid S3 URI
    Given ingest_config_master row has s3_vendor_path = "invalid_path"
    When the script runs
    Then it should fail with error message "Invalid S3 URI in configuration: invalid_path"

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if file_name is null or empty in Vendor S3 listing
    Given the Vendor S3 folder contains a file with file_name = null
    When the script runs
    Then it should skip this file

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if file_name is null or empty in Purgo or Archive S3 listing
    Given the Purgo S3 folder contains a file with file_name = null
    When the script runs
    Then it should not consider this file for matching

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if file_name in Vendor S3 matches (case-sensitive, full match) a file in either Purgo or Archive S3
    Given the Vendor S3 folder contains "fileD.csv"
    And the Purgo S3 folder contains "fileD.csv"
    And the Archive S3 folder contains "fileE.csv"
    When the script runs
    Then it should not transfer "fileD.csv"

  Scenario: Transfer files for all active configurations in ingest_config_master
    Given ingest_config_master contains:
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path              | s3_landing_path              | s3_archive_path              | active_flag |
      | 10        | s3://vendor-bucket/folderA/ | s3://purgo-bucket/landingA/  | s3://purgo-bucket/archiveA/  | A           |
      | 11        | s3://vendor-bucket/folderB/ | s3://purgo-bucket/landingB/  | s3://purgo-bucket/archiveB/  | A           |
    And each Vendor S3 folder contains files not present in their respective Purgo or Archive S3 folders
    When the script runs
    Then it should transfer eligible files for both config_id 10 and 11

  Scenario: Do not transfer files for configurations with active_flag not equal to "A"
    Given ingest_config_master contains:
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path              | s3_landing_path              | s3_archive_path              | active_flag |
      | 12        | s3://vendor-bucket/folderC/ | s3://purgo-bucket/landingC/  | s3://purgo-bucket/archiveC/  | I           |
    When the script runs
    Then it should not process config_id 12

  Scenario: Error if file transfer to Purgo S3 fails due to insufficient permissions
    Given the script attempts to transfer "fileF.csv" and receives "403 Forbidden"
    When the script processes the file
    Then it should log error "Failed to transfer fileF.csv: 403 Forbidden"
    And the file should not be present in the Purgo S3 folder

  Scenario: Error if file transfer to Purgo S3 fails due to missing destination bucket
    Given the script attempts to transfer "fileG.csv" and receives "NoSuchBucket"
    When the script processes the file
    Then it should log error "Failed to transfer fileG.csv: NoSuchBucket"
    And the file should not be present in the Purgo S3 folder

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if file_name in Vendor S3 is a duplicate (appears more than once)
    Given the Vendor S3 folder contains:
      | file_name     |
      | fileH.csv     |
      | fileH.csv     |
    When the script runs
    Then it should transfer "fileH.csv" only once

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if file_name in Vendor S3 is already present in both Purgo and Archive S3
    Given the Vendor S3 folder contains "fileI.csv"
    And the Purgo S3 folder contains "fileI.csv"
    And the Archive S3 folder contains "fileI.csv"
    When the script runs
    Then it should not transfer "fileI.csv"

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if file_name in Vendor S3 is present in Archive S3 but not in Purgo S3
    Given the Vendor S3 folder contains "fileJ.csv"
    And the Purgo S3 folder does not contain "fileJ.csv"
    And the Archive S3 folder contains "fileJ.csv"
    When the script runs
    Then it should not transfer "fileJ.csv"

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if file_name in Vendor S3 is present in Purgo S3 but not in Archive S3
    Given the Vendor S3 folder contains "fileK.csv"
    And the Purgo S3 folder contains "fileK.csv"
    And the Archive S3 folder does not contain "fileK.csv"
    When the script runs
    Then it should not transfer "fileK.csv"

  Scenario: Transfer file if file_name in Vendor S3 is not present in either Purgo S3 or Archive S3
    Given the Vendor S3 folder contains "fileL.csv"
    And the Purgo S3 folder does not contain "fileL.csv"
    And the Archive S3 folder does not contain "fileL.csv"
    When the script runs
    Then it should transfer "fileL.csv"

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if active_flag is not "A" (case-sensitive)
    Given ingest_config_master row has active_flag = "a"
    When the script runs
    Then it should not process this configuration

  Scenario: Error if s3_vendor_path, s3_landing_path, or s3_archive_path is empty string
    Given ingest_config_master row has s3_vendor_path = ""
    When the script runs
    Then it should fail with error message "S3 path columns (s3_vendor_path, s3_landing_path, s3_archive_path) must not be empty for active configuration"
